1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:30,300
Alright, you head to the sand pit, I'll take the riverbank.

3
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,220
Those are most likely Training

4
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,660
In those two spots.

5
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,030
I propose we set up a Friendly

6
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,020
Exhibition Match with Jianghai Team.

7
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:38,430
One, it can serve as

8
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,900
A warm-up for the Fall Yo-Yo Tournament.

9
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,820
And two, it'll let us test out

10
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,740
how effective each of our Teams' Training has been.

11
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,140
I've been wanting to go head-to-head
with Chengnan Team for so long.

12
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,020
Coach, Chengnan Team has been targeting us the whole time.

13
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:50,910
And now out of nowhere, they propose
a Friendly Exhibition Match?

14
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,380
That doesn't fit their style at all.

15
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:53,820
There's gotta be a trap.

16
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,740
I know Coach Sarah very well.

17
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,660
She would never do something like that.

18
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Episode 18

19
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,820
Didn't she already say that?

20
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,220
She knows her Players inside and out.

21
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:11,100
Besides, this Exhibition Match

22
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,540
was her idea in the first place.

23
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,390
If you suspect her Players have bad intentions,

24
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,860
isn't that the same as doubting her?

25
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,260
Who wouldn't feel hurt by that?

26
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,660
I'm just trying to get to the bottom of this.

27
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,060
But you're making things way too complicated.

28
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:28,860
Yeah, we're rivals with Chengnan Team,

29
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,780
but we're still Sister Schools.

30
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:34,140
There's no need to be so paranoid.

31
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,540
Coach, you're right.

32
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:39,420
But I'm just not used to this kind of thing back home.

33
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:40,380
All this bias,

34
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:43,740
that lets people ignore the rules of Competition.

35
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:44,700
Bias?

36
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:49,980
Do you really think I'm being biased?

37
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,720
Maybe just a little.

38
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:54,780
Leo.

39
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:59,070
I'm not doing this because

40
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:01,980
Coach Sarah and I went to the same School.

41
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:04,350
It's because I understand and trust her.

42
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,310
You get that?

43
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,260
I'm not doubting Coach Sarah. I just...

44
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,140
Alright, that's enough on this.

45
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,230
From now on, whether it's during Training time

46
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,220
or break time,

47
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,140
if any of you want to leave the Team,

48
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:25,020
you have to get my permission first.

49
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,990
Just so we can avoid any unnecessary misunderstandings.

50
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,820
Is that clear?

51
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:31,740
Crystal clear.

52
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,180
Alright, dismissed.

53
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,580
Get back to Training.

54
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,310
This is the plan I came up with

55
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,300
for this Exhibition Match.

56
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:07,710
Everyone understand?

57
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:08,700
Got it.

58
00:04:09,430 --> 00:04:10,140
Awesome!

59
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,580
We finally get to use our Signature Moves!

60
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,020
I can't wait for this Match to start.

61
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,420
We're gonna shake things up and blow them away!

62
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,820
When you're the one Competing,

63
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,740
you're the easiest one to draw attention to.

64
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,150
Can't help it.

65
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,620
Captain, just trust me.

66
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,500
Yeah, we trust that your skills are... a little weaker.

67
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:27,760
So you go first, and if you lose,
I'll step in and back you up.

68
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:29,120
Alright, alright.

69
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,570
At a crucial moment like this,

70
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:32,710
let's stop bickering over this childish stuff.

71
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:35,580
If no one has any objections,

72
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,500
then we'll proceed with this plan.

73
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,390
The Captain's plan is definitely solid.

74
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,340
Just give the word and we'll follow your lead.

75
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:44,700
I disagree.

76
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,580
This plan doesn't make sense.

77
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:50,760
If we go with this, Jianghai Team's
going to have a really hard time winning.

78
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:51,420
Huh?

79
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,190
Because Chengnan Team has likely

80
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:58,110
already figured out all of our Signature Moves.

81
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,540
We need to change up our Techniques
if we want to secure a win.

82
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,460
But I've already perfected my Signature Move!

83
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:06,780
But I think Leo's suggestion is the safer bet.

84
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,630
Everyone can just learn a variation

85
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,700
on top of their original Signature Move.

86
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,900
That way, even if Chengnan Team knows our moves,

87
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,210
they won't have time to adjust their own strategy.

88
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:18,300
Exactly. I mean, it might be a bit harder this way,

89
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,670
but as long as we really push ourselves,

90
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,620
we can definitely get it done in time.

91
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:25,020
Don't just blindly follow whatever Leo says.

92
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,940
Trying to learn new variations now?

93
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,790
There's no way it'll be as stable as
just using our original Signature Moves.

94
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,750
But if the other Team

95
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:32,220
has already figured out our Signature Moves,

96
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,620
the more stable and predictable we are,

97
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:37,020
the easier we make it for them to control the whole Match.

98
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,420
Leo, you are way too full of yourself.

99
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,820
Just because you have a little suspicion,

100
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:43,710
you want us to change our Signature Moves

101
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,180
and destroy our entire plan?

102
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:47,100
You just like to hear yourself talk!

103
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:50,430
Yeah, there's no need for you

104
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,380
to always deliberately go against the Captain.

105
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:55,260
Just to show off how "capable" you think you are?

106
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:58,140
I'm criticizing the plan, not the person.

107
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,030
Enough! I'm the Captain,

108
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,500
I get to decide the plan.

109
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,640
But a plan has to be reasonable before we can carry it out!

110
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,940
Leo, you're getting way too arrogant!

111
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,140
The Captain's already made himself perfectly clear,

112
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,060
and you're still running your mouth?

113
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:13,500
Okay, let's stop fighting.

114
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,420
Let's just ask the Coach.

115
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,260
Leo.

116
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:22,140
You won't accept the Captain's plan,

117
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,020
and you won't listen to what your Coach says either.

118
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:28,830
Aren't you being a little bit...

119
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:32,220
Coach, I'm standing by my opinion
because there's a reason for it.

120
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:35,580
Everyone thinks their own opinion makes sense.

121
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,460
But sometimes you have to

122
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,380
Listen to other people's opinions.

123
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,740
Just because you're the most skilled

124
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,620
doesn't mean you can just ignore the Team's decisions.

125
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:51,420
That's just you trying to be some lone Hero.

126
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,740
I'm still standing by my own opinion.

127
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,660
I don't agree with this plan.

128
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:01,020
Coach, I'm leaving.

129
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,420
Hey.

130
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,220
Leo.

131
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,100
Don't be mad.

132
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,940
The Coach didn't really mean what he said.

133
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:32,700
Everyone's just trying to do
what's best for Jianghai Team.

134
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:36,210
But you should watch what you say sometimes, you know?

135
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,420
I don't like Cheese either,

136
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,780
but it's still School property, right?

137
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,220
Right, right, right.

138
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:59,100
And anyway, stealing Cheese is one thing,

139
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,500
but ruining your own Character is way worse.

140
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:03,900
Stealing is just a despicable act.

141
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,820
It's absolutely intolerable.

142
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:08,580
Yeah, we won't tolerate it.

143
00:08:08,990 --> 00:08:11,580
And this matter, I'm going to get to the bottom of it.

144
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:14,460
And if it turns out it was one of our Players,

145
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,790
we will punish them severely.

146
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,780
No leniency.

147
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,180
They should be firmly expelled.

148
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,100
Expelled?

149
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,220
Did everyone hear that clearly?

150
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:46,620
This time, I'm going to deal with this very seriously.

151
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,380
Why are you all looking at me? It wasn't me.

152
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,780
Major suspect.

153
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:56,220
No matter who it was,

154
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:59,070
if they just come clean and confess,

155
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,060
there might still be a chance.

156
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,940
Otherwise, once we find out who did it,
they'll be expelled without question.

157
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:06,300
Did you hear that?!

158
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:09,660
Why are you pushing me? I told you, I didn't do it!

159
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,580
Ever since I wrote that self-reflection last time,

160
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,020
I've completely changed my ways.

161
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,380
Besides, I'm trying to lose weight anyway.

162
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:21,180
If it wasn't you, it wasn't you. Why are you crying?

163
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,060
With everyone looking at me like that,

164
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,460
even I'm starting to think I actually did it!

165
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:29,340
So was it you or not?!

166
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,260
No, no, no, it wasn't me!

167
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:37,980
Alright. We can't go around accusing innocent people.

168
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,610
But we absolutely can't let the real thief get away either.

169
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:42,780
To clear everyone's name,

170
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:45,180
every single Team Member is going to be searched.

171
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:32,700
What's wrong?

172
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:37,020
Leo.

173
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:42,300
The Camp kitchen had some Cheese go missing,

174
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:45,180
and they suspect one of our Players took it.

175
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:48,060
So everyone's being searched right now.

176
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:49,980
We've all been searched already.

177
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,340
It's just down to you and Mini now.

178
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:56,680
Leo. Mini.

179
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,580
Are you two willing to be searched?

180
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:01,310
No problem.

181
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,940
Yeah, that's fine.

182
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:18,780
What is this?

183
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:24,540
How did the Cheese end up in my bag?

184
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:25,500
You're asking us?

185
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,310
We should be asking you.

186
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:31,260
Leo, just drop the act already.

187
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,660
Coach, I didn't take it.

188
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:36,060
Good thing we got to the bottom of this.

189
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:37,020
Otherwise,

190
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:39,420
I could have a million mouths and
still never clear my name.

191
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:42,300
So you think I'm the one who took the Cheese?

192
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,700
Well, isn't it obvious?

193
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:46,620
You're the only one on this whole Team, Leo,

194
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,060
who even likes eating that stuff.

195
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:51,030
That's impossible. Leo's not like that.

196
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:53,820
We don't want to believe it either.

197
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:54,780
But,

198
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:57,180
the Cheese was found right in Leo's own backpack.

199
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:58,620
No matter how much you defend him,

200
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:00,540
you can't just ignore the facts.

201
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:04,380
Yeah! And remember, after Leo
beat that Masked Guy the other day,

202
00:12:04,740 --> 00:12:06,300
he specifically asked for a Cheese Sandwich!

203
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,220
Yeah, yeah, I remember that too.

204
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,440
Well, don't you have great memory.

205
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:12,060
If you don't talk, nobody's gonna think you're mute.

206
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:15,420
Coach, do you really think I stole it too?

207
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:18,780
Then how do you explain this?

208
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:20,700
I have no idea how that happened.

209
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:22,140
But I really didn't take that Cheese.

210
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:25,500
Well, then someone must be framing Leo.

211
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:26,940
Mickey.

212
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:30,780
You and your Sister are always defending Leo.

213
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:33,180
We get it.

214
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,100
But by saying that, you're just trying to

215
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:36,820
pin the blame on the rest of us.

216
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,900
Isn't that going a little too far?

217
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:43,260
Yeah! Now you've got everyone
all paranoid and on edge.

218
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:45,660
My heart's still pounding like crazy right now!

219
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:49,280
Coach, we've all been together as a Team for so long now.

220
00:12:50,290 --> 00:12:53,860
Everyone here knows exactly what kind of person Leo is.
We've all seen it with our own eyes.

221
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:56,700
But we haven't known him nearly
as long as you two have.

222
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,100
Monica.

223
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:01,020
Leo's always been really nice to you, too.

224
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:02,940
He was just helping you practice the other day!

225
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,340
That's completely different.

226
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:07,740
This is a matter of principle.

227
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:11,580
Everything we do has to be guided by principles.

228
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,500
Isn't that right?

229
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:15,900
Leo, why don't you explain yourself?

230
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,820
Stop always having other people stick up for you.

231
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:20,220
And don't make the whole Team take the fall with you!

232
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,060
I don't know what the rest of you are thinking,

233
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:25,980
but I did not steal any Cheese.

234
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:27,420
There's nothing more for me to explain.

235
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,340
Leo!

236
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:30,780
What kind of attitude is that?

237
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,660
I'm so disappointed in you.

238
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,020
I've always thought

239
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:39,270
you were an honest and upright kid.

240
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:41,820
Someone who'd own up to their actions like a Man.

241
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,180
I never expected you to be like this.

242
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,980
Since no one here trusts me,

243
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:53,340
since you all think I've dragged the
Team's name through the mud,

244
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,700
then I can just quit Jianghai Team.

245
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:03,390
Coach, please, you have to say something!

246
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,380
Mini!

247
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:05,820
I've said this before.

248
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:08,320
I will not tolerate anything that damages
the reputation of Jianghai Team.

249
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:09,660
Or anyone!

250
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,100
Coach!

251
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,300
Leo, wait a second.

252
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:36,940
Go away.

253
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:40,350
Teddy.

254
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:40,860
Get out of here!

255
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:42,300
How could you?

256
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Teddy,

257
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,500
Was it you who put that Cheese in Leo's bag?

258
00:14:59,510 --> 00:15:00,840
What?

259
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Yes, it was me.

260
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:06,300
How could you do this?!

261
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,630
I did it all for you!

262
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:10,620
What do you mean, "for me"?

263
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:13,020
When did I ever ask you to do something like this?

264
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,420
I didn't plan it at first.

265
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,820
I was just wandering around the kitchen,

266
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:21,180
thinking I'd find some leftover
steamed buns or something.

267
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:24,060
But then I happened to stumble across
this huge block of Cheese.

268
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,940
And the only one on this whole
Team who loves that stuff is Leo.

269
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:30,300
So I figured, this had to be fate.

270
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:34,140
So I just improvised. I adapted to the circumstances.

271
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:37,980
I used what was available and...
"liberated" that block of Cheese,

272
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:41,340
and I slipped it right into Leo's backpack.

273
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:42,780
Enough, Teddy!

274
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:45,480
What do you mean, "used what was available"? What "fate"?

275
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:48,030
That was stealing! And you framed someone for it!

276
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:49,980
Hold on! You're wrong about that.

277
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:52,860
In my opinion, any act of "liberation"

278
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:55,740
first comes from a sense of
personal connection to the object.

279
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:59,620
Only then does the motivation arise,
and finally, the act itself.

280
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:01,200
So how can you call that stealing?

281
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,380
Alright, Alright, Teddy, enough!

282
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:05,820
I know you were trying to help me.

283
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:07,740
But don't you think this was going way too far?

284
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:10,140
Now you've dragged me into having to cover for you!

285
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:13,020
"Too far"? What's that supposed to mean?

286
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:15,870
That Leo guy, in front of the whole Team,

287
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:19,100
showing you, the Captain, absolutely no respect—
is that not "too far"?

288
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,190
He's always acting like

289
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,390
he's some big shot just because
he came back from America.

290
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,060
Isn't that "too far"?

291
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:26,910
And the way he's always doting on Mini,

292
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,860
way more than he should. Isn't that "too far," too?

293
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,260
Hey! Leave Mini out of this!

294
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:33,180
Hmph. Even I couldn't stand watching that.

295
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:36,060
Anyway, we already got what we wanted.

296
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,980
The Coach has made his decision.

297
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:39,900
What's with you getting all soft-hearted now?

298
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:42,780
This isn't what I wanted.

299
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:45,660
I wanted Leo to leave with no hard feelings,
completely convinced.

300
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:46,620
But now?

301
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,770
What's done is done.

302
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:52,380
If you go and blab about this,

303
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,500
Both of us will be out of Jianghai Team for good!

304
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:58,160
Alright, my dear Captain.

305
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,980
As long as Jianghai Team can beat
Chengnan Team in this match,

306
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:03,420
No one will dare question you then.

307
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:05,820
This is your chance!

308
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,660
Fine.

309
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,100
I guess it has to be this way.

310
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,700
Of course I believe you. I know you didn't do this.

311
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:36,540
But you can't just be so rash.

312
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:42,300
Let's go talk to Coach Tony again and
explain everything properly.

313
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:45,180
Once everyone's had a chance to cool down,

314
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:48,060
we'll get to the bottom of this eventually.

315
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:53,340
Things have already gotten this far.

316
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:55,260
What's the point of explaining anything now?

317
00:17:57,160 --> 00:18:00,060
I have no way to defend myself.

318
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:01,500
I have no proof that I'm innocent,

319
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:03,420
and I can't prove someone else did it either.

320
00:18:04,540 --> 00:18:06,780
If there's no proof, then we'll just go find some!

321
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:13,020
But you can't just swallow this
injustice and accept it by staying quiet!

322
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:19,860
Even the Coach looks at me differently now.

323
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:24,060
There's no point in me staying here anymore.

324
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,900
Coach Tony might have a short temper,

325
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:31,260
but he's definitely not a fool.

326
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:35,980
Can we just go try one more time? Please?

327
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:11,100
No, Mickey!

328
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,460
If I let Leo off the hook this time,

329
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:17,340
what am I supposed to do the next time
someone else messes up?

330
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,180
I've said it over and over again, discipline is everything!

331
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:22,620
I want to forge this Team

332
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:24,540
into something as strong as the Military,

333
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:26,960
with an Iron will and Iron discipline.

334
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:29,340
Anyone who breaks the rules

335
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:31,260
has to face severe punishment.

336
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,180
Besides,

337
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,580
we already have the example of what happened with Chuck.

338
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:37,020
But Coach!

339
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:39,420
If Leo's not on the Team anymore,

340
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:42,300
our match against Chengnan Team is
going to be in serious jeopardy!

341
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,540
I'd rather lose a single match

342
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:52,380
and lose a great Yo-Yo player

343
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:54,300
than keep a Team Member

344
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:56,670
who has no integrity or character!

345
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:57,630
But Coach!

346
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:59,550
I'm telling you, I believe

347
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:01,020
that Leo had nothing to do with this!

348
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:02,940
Mickey.

349
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:05,740
You need to have proof before
you say something like that.

350
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:08,220
You can't just go on blind faith.

351
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:09,660
Alright?

352
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:13,020
Right now, your job is to go straight back to bed.

353
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:16,350
And stop trying to plead Leo's case. Just go.

354
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,340
Coach!

355
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:18,300
Go on.

356
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:41,350
So, what are you planning to do after you leave?

357
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:45,660
I came back from America

358
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:48,270
hoping to broaden my horizons.

359
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:49,980
I wanted to take my Yo-Yo skills to the next level.

360
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:52,380
My Dad told me

361
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:55,260
that I should draw from the essence
of traditional Chinese culture.

362
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:59,100
So I plan to use the spiritual
intent found in Eastern philosophy

363
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:01,500
to challenge the Western concept of pure speed.

364
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:04,350
It'll be a contest between

365
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:06,300
Absolute time and Relative time.

366
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:08,220
Yeah, yeah, that's exactly right! You nailed it!

367
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,900
But I'm getting off topic. Let's not talk about that now.

368
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:19,740
I think this time I've spent back home,

369
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,950
it's probably going to help me out a lot down the road.

370
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
But for now,

371
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,840
it's time for me to go.

